# line does and Tools/NeoText for where the convention started.
#
# About belongs with the documentation rather than with the tools: it
# says what this is and what version it is, which is the first thing
# anyone reading Core/Docs wants to be told, and the drawer is where
# they are standing when they want it.  Filed here it opens beside the
# guide and the readme, which is where the answer to "what is this?"
# ought to live.
#
# It is still on the start menu as well -- this is one more way to it,
# not the only one.

